# ccl78 — the TENANT REGISTRY of this deployment.
#
# The jar enables no tenant: a start that finds no registry is refused
#   ("REFUSING TO START: no tenant is enabled. …").
# These three lines are what the jar itself carried until now. Put them into
#     <the service's working directory>/config/application.properties
# on the box (Quarkus reads that file over the jar's own). For deploy-ccl-prod.sh the working directory
# is the unit's WorkingDirectory — /opt/billing/app when the unit runs the jar from there — so the file is
#     /opt/billing/app/config/application.properties
# The deploy script replaces app/, lib/, quarkus/ and quarkus-run.jar only: a config/ directory stays.
#
# Do it BEFORE the first build that enables no tenant is deployed. If it is forgotten the service does
# not start, and deploy-ccl-prod.sh rolls back to the previous build by itself (its health check).
#
# If the box already has a config/application.properties with billing.tenants[...] lines of its own,
# it needs nothing: this file changes nothing for it.
billing.tenants[0].name=ccl78
billing.tenants[0].enabled=true
billing.tenants[0].profile=dev
